      "publicIdentifier": "michael-balog-9b81561",
      "headline": "Technical Art Director, Physics at Epic Games",
      "about": "I'm a Technical Art Director for Physics at Epic Games, where I work within the UE Engine Lab Group. Over the course of my time at Epic, I've led the Technical Animation, Mocap, and Pipeline Development departments, served as Director of Animation Technology, collaborated with the Special Projects Team, and on titles including Paragon and Lego Fortnite. My current focus is driving new Chaos/Physics features in Unreal Engine 5 — pushing the boundaries of what real-time physics can do in games. Before joining Epic, I spent 17 years in the VFX industry at Industrial Light and Magic, where I supervised nine projects with teams of up to 30 artists and contributed to more than 30 films. Those credits include some of the most iconic franchises in cinema — Star Wars, Harry Potter, Transformers, and Pacific Rim — with my core expertise in creature simulation, rigging, and RBD destruction. Of everything I worked on, the Dementors in Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban remain a personal favorite: technically demanding to build, but deeply satisfying to see come to life on screen. I've been fortunate to work alongside exceptional artists, lead talented teams, and play a meaningful role in shaping films and games that have left a lasting mark on the entertainment industry.EPICDepartments Managed:Tech Art - PhysicsTechnical Animation MocapPipeline DevelopmentProjects:Lego FortniteFortniteParagonThe Matrix Awakens - DemoValley of the Ancient - DemoChaos Destruction - DemoFortnite Release Trailer - Real-Time TrailerILMCreature/RBD Destruction Supervisor• Manage teams of visual effects artists• Work with production to provide solutions to scheduling• Bid projects• Interview and hire artists• Develop FX setups for shot work• Work with artists to effectively maintain technical direction with their shots• Troubleshoot and devise solutions to maintain workflow and pipeline• Work with RND to develop new tools and pipeline• Public relations events (e.g. Siggraph panels, Job Fares, etc.)• Shot workCreature Technical Director• RBD sims, creatures and environment• Rigging• Asset management• Creature setups, skinning, cloth, hair, flesh• Shot finaling, sims and shape correctives• ModelingResource Assistant• Managed disk space• Loaded and backed up data",
